Step 1: Clone the Repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/vishakha2121/ai-universal-decision-engine.git
cd ai-universal-decision-engine
Step 2: Setup Backend
bash
cd backend
python -m venv venv

# Activate virtualenv
# On Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate
# On macOS/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
Create .env file inside backend/:

env
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_actual_gemini_api_key_here
DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/decision_engine.db
Step 3: Initialize Database
bash
python database.py
(This will create the SQLite file and all tables automatically.)

Step 4: Run Backend
bash
uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000
Backend runs at: http://localhost:8000
API Docs (Swagger): http://localhost:8000/docs

Step 5: Setup Frontend
Open a new terminal:

bash
cd frontend
npm install
Create .env file inside frontend/:

env
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
Step 6: Run Frontend
bash
npm run dev
Frontend runs at: http://localhost:5173

14. Environment Variables
Backend (.env)
Variable	Description
GEMINI_API_KEY	Your Google Gemini API key
DATABASE_URL	SQLite path (default: sqlite:///./data/decision_engine.db)
LOG_LEVEL	INFO / DEBUG / ERROR
CORS_ORIGINS	Allowed origins (default: http://localhost:5173)
Frontend (.env)
Variable	Description
VITE_API_BASE_URL	Backend URL (default: http://localhost:8000)
15. Running the Application
Full flow:

Start backend: uvicorn main:app --reload --port 8000

Start frontend: npm run dev

Open browser: http://localhost:5173

Pick a domain → Enter a query → Click "Solve"

Watch the reasoning trace animate step-by-step

See the final decision + confidence meter

16. Example Use Cases
💰 Finance
"Should I approve a loan of ₹5,00,000 for a customer with ₹60,000/month income and 680 credit score?"

Output:

Step 1: Input validation ✓

Step 2: DTI = 8.33 → Too high ⚠️

Step 3: Credit score below 700 threshold ⚠️

Verdict: REJECT (Confidence: 85%)

🏥 Medicine
"Patient has fever, headache, and body ache for 3 days. What could it be?"

Output:

Step 1: Extract symptoms

Step 2: Match against symptom-disease DB

Step 3: Rule check for red-flag combinations

Verdict: Possible viral fever (Confidence: 70%) — recommend doctor consultation

🚚 Logistics
"Estimate delivery time from Delhi to Jaipur for a 5-ton truck."

Output:

Step 1: Distance = 280 km

Step 2: Truck speed (avg 50 km/h)

Step 3: Estimated time = 5.6 hours + breaks

Verdict: ~6.5 hours (Confidence: 90%)

17. Design Principles
Principle	How It's Applied
Single Responsibility	Every reasoner, detector, scorer has one job
Open/Closed	Add new domains/strategies without touching core
Strategy Pattern	Reasoners are interchangeable via BaseReasoner
Dependency Injection	Engine receives reasoners via constructor
Fail-safe Fallback	Gemini fails → rule-based takes over
Explicit over Implicit	Full reasoning trace, not hidden logic
DRY	Shared validators, prompt builders
18. Why This Project Stands Out
Explainability First — Most student projects only return answers. This one returns reasoning.

True Modularity — Adding a 6th domain = add one folder. Zero core edits.

Real Strategy Pattern — Not just a buzzword, actually implemented via BaseReasoner.

Hybrid Intelligence — Rule-based + Formula + LLM. Not just an API wrapper.

Full-Stack Implementation — React UI + FastAPI backend + SQLite DB + LLM integration.

Trace Persistence — Every step is stored in the DB — audit-ready.

Confidence Scoring — System self-evaluates its own certainty.

Beautiful UI — Animated trace viewer, glassmorphism cards, dark theme.

Interview-Friendly — The architecture demonstrates design pattern mastery.

Honest Scope — Clearly marked as practice, not production.

19. Roadmap
Future enhancements (post-practice):

□ User authentication
□ Multi-language support
□ Voice input via Web Speech API
□ PDF export of reasoning traces
□ Fine-tuned local LLM for offline mode
□ Custom domain plugins via JSON
□ Dockerize for easy deployment
□ Unit test coverage report
20. Known Limitations
Not production-grade — No auth, no rate limiting, no HTTPS.

Gemini free tier rate limits — Approx. 15 requests/minute.

SQLite concurrency — Single-writer limitation (fine for practice).

No unit tests yet — Planned for future.

No caching layer — Every request hits Gemini when needed.

Rule-based reasoning is simplistic — Enough to demonstrate the concept, not real finance/medicine standards.

No legal compliance — Not suitable for actual financial/medical advice.

